[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100691 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869}] :question/id #uuid "da92ef6c-cb0b-5a4c-9a0d-0f0a9db19616" :question/math-academy-id "e-4403" :question/problem "Let\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}19 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & -1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- **I.** The product $A\\times B$ is well defined\n\n- **II.** The product $B\\times A$ is well defined" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, and $B$ is a $2 \\times 3$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2 \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{2}}}{A} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{2}} \\times 3}{B} = \n\t{\\color{green}\\text{well defined}}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $B$ and $2$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{2 \\times \\color{red}{3}}{B} \\underset{\\color{red}\\neq}{\\times} \\underset{{\\color{red}2} \\times 2}{A} = {\\color{red}\\text{undefined}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, statement I is true, while statement II is false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101319 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eee15b20-7670-503f-971f-d56fd86f8528" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448504} {:answer/id #uuid "8e36cc5c-ee04-5d14-93c0-5ec4fd6754bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448505}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e36cc5c-ee04-5d14-93c0-5ec4fd6754bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448505} :answer-field/id #uuid "73a25775-ae2f-598a-be5f-116f1c5257d3" :answer-field/key "The product $AB$ is well defined." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449292} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a98bec2-fd5b-577d-b1a2-de624a75c4de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448506} {:answer/id #uuid "8f344679-285a-5a78-87d1-893db3de166d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448507}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a98bec2-fd5b-577d-b1a2-de624a75c4de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448506} :answer-field/id #uuid "72b90ee4-8516-5880-9f21-2235262ae0b8" :answer-field/key "The product $BA$ is well defined." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449293} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69c941f3-afcf-5dca-a631-aac8dfb757b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448508} {:answer/id #uuid "384c1599-b211-55de-9dff-459dd6139d8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "384c1599-b211-55de-9dff-459dd6139d8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448509} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa235668-87f9-5d4c-8f5d-dd9e00466bf2" :answer-field/key "The product $AC$ is well defined." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449294}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9258b6d8-3a2c-54d4-bc2f-8b9ea4ccd825" :question/math-academy-id "q-22063" :question/problem "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 7 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $A,B,$ and $C?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix, $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3\\times 1$ column vector\n\nThere are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $B$ and $3$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{B}_{3\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{A}_{3\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $C.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $C,$ the matrices $A$ and $C$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{C}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 1}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nThe products $AB$ and $AC$ are well defined. The product $BA$ is undefined."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101409 :knowledge-point/_questions 