45485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "12577a38-9f6c-5807-b07b-3944030b826c" :question/math-academy-id "q-22056" :question/problem "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$S=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 & 8\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$T=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $R,S,$ and $T?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that $R$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix, $S$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix, and $T$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere are $4$ columns in $S$ and $4$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ equals the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $S$ and $R$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{✓}{R}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $R$ and $2$ rows in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ equals the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $R$ and $S$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{S}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $4$ columns in $S$ and $3$ rows in $T.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $T,$ the matrices $S$ and $T$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{2\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{T}_{3\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nThe products $SR$ and $RS$ are well defined. The product $ST$ is undefined."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290371 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d3c92a8-562e-563a-8881-3b32d1e12722" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218604