0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$N=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $L,M,$ and $N?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that $L$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, $M$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, and $N$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere are $3$ columns in $M$ and $2$ rows in $L.$ Since the number of columns in $M$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $L,$ the matrices $M$ and $L$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{M}_{2\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{L}_{2\\times 3}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $3$ columns in $M$ and $3$ rows in $N.$ Since the number of columns in $M$ equals the number of rows in $N,$ the matrices $M$ and $N$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{M}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{N}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $3$ columns in $L$ and $3$ rows in $N.$ Since the number of columns in $L$ equals the number of rows in $N,$ the matrices $L$ and $N$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{L}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\times }_{✓}{N}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nThe products $MN$ and $LN$ are well defined. The product $ML$ is undefined."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329647 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b747550b-0a4a-5f3d-86b4-30ddaca87768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450648} {:answer/id #uuid "f90dfbaa-1eb7-5028-8821-63442d778562" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uui